  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating and supporting a Womens&#x2019; Policy Action Forum advocating for the removal of barriers to women&#x2019;s economic empowerment.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to create a robust policy action group, &#x201c;Women&#x2019;s Policy Action Forum&#x201d; (WPAF), who can advocate for policy reforms aimed at enabling women&#x2019;s economic empowerment. The proposed group will comprise representatives from Civil Society Organizations, policymakers and women leaders that form a strong ongoing lobby on behalf of women. WPAF will engage various stakeholders in raising awareness, creating a platform for consensus on reform, and engaging in discussions with key policymakers pushing for action on reform. The group will advocate for evidence-based policy reform proposals developed by Advocata Institute in areas such as reforming discriminatory labour laws and regulations, reducing taxes and tariffs that disproportionately affect women, and implementation of gender sensitive public policy. Reducing the barriers women face in entering the labour force will allow women in the informal sector to join the formal labour force and thereby enjoy the same benefits. These reforms will aim to improve the livelihood of economically disadvantaged women by reducing the barriers to their economic empowerment. Advocata Institute will provide research, advocacy and logistical support to the group in the following ways: ? Provide program support to the day to day functioning of the Women&#x2019;s Policy Action Forum. ? Conduct the research needed on a range of potential issues that looks into legal and public policy barriers to women&#x2019;s economic empowerment. ? Provide WPAF policy briefs and other materials necessary for evidence-based advocacy on the identified issues.</narrative>
  </description>
